guamp: frame trace writer (frames.trace, cpu.profile) only in backboardd

The paths are in com.apple.backboardd caches; every other Metal client (gpu-all) retried the open every 400 ms and drew
repeated sandbox denies. NMB_TRACE_ALL=1 restores the old behaviour.

diff --git a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
index 0e5055e..e353da4 100644
--- a/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
+++ b/NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm
@@ -302,6 +302,13 @@ static void sampleWriteProfile(uint32_t &consumed,int &fd,const char *const *pat
 static void traceStartWriter() {
  bool expected=false;
  if(!gTraceStarted.compare_exchange_strong(expected,true))return;
+ // guamp (UniXNU-guamp patches/adreno-metal/0007): frames.trace and cpu.profile live in backboardd's own cache directory; any other
+ // process (gpu-all clients, sandboxed widgets and posters) was denied the open every 400 ms for its whole life (sandbox deny storm,
+ // a sampling profiler thread for nothing). Only the render server writes them; NMB_TRACE_ALL=1 restores the old behaviour.
+ {
+  const char *name=getprogname();const char *all=getenv("NMB_TRACE_ALL");
+  if(!(all && strtoul(all,nullptr,0)) && !(name && strcmp(name,"backboardd")==0))return;
+ }
  std::thread([]{
   pthread_setname_np("frame-trace");
   int fd=-1;
